    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d409-a1">

                <pb facs="0769" n="659" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg659"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 456.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Colonel Stewart to
                        Sir H. D. Wolff.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tauris</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps">Tabreez</hi>)</placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1890-05-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 23, 1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Her Britannic Majesty’s
                        Minister</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Teheran:</hi></p>
                <p>The wife of Rev. J. Wright, American missionary here, was stabbed by an Armenian.
                    She is very dangerously wounded and is in a critical condition. I am doing
                    everything to get assassin, who fled, arrested.</p>
                <p>Governor before my arrival gave no assistance, but is now trying hard to arrest
                    assassin.</p>
                <p>Mrs. Wright is by birth a Nestorian. Please inform American minister.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stewart.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
